{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q55866501","formula":"VN","hill":"NV","elements":["N","V"],"composition":{"N":1.0,"V":1.0},"names":{"en":"Uakitite"},"descriptions":{"en":"Uakitite is a mineral found in a single meteorite on Earth, called the Uakit meteorite, that fell in the Bauntovsky Evenkiysky District, in Republic of Buryatia, Russia. It was named after the region in which it was found, Uakit. Uakitite is composed of vanadium nitride, a chemical compound of vanadium and nitrogen with formula VN. While the majority of the meteorite is composed of an iron and nickel alloy called kamacite, a small percentage of the meteorite contains minerals that are only found in space, including uakitite."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1018027","atoms":20,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[2.734,0.0,0.0],[-1.367,2.368,0.0],[0.0,0.0,2.641]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.367,"y":0.789,"z":0.0,"el":"V"},{"x":1.367,"y":0.789,"z":5.283,"el":"V"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.578,"z":1.321,"el":"N"},{"x":1.367,"y":0.789,"z":2.641,"el":"V"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.578,"z":3.962,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.157,"z":0.0,"el":"V"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.157,"z":5.283,"el":"V"},{"x":-1.367,"y":3.946,"z":1.321,"el":"N"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.157,"z":2.641,"el":"V"},{"x":-1.367,"y":3.946,"z":3.962,"el":"N"},{"x":4.101,"y":0.789,"z":0.0,"el":"V"},{"x":4.101,"y":0.789,"z":5.283,"el":"V"},{"x":2.734,"y":1.578,"z":1.321,"el":"N"},{"x":4.101,"y":0.789,"z":2.641,"el":"V"},{"x":2.734,"y":1.578,"z":3.962,"el":"N"},{"x":2.734,"y":3.157,"z":0.0,"el":"V"},{"x":2.734,"y":3.157,"z":5.283,"el":"V"},{"x":1.367,"y":3.946,"z":1.321,"el":"N"},{"x":2.734,"y":3.157,"z":2.641,"el":"V"},{"x":1.367,"y":3.946,"z":3.962,"el":"N"}],"bonds":[[4,8,1],[5,7,1],[5,17,1],[7,8,